\f0\b\fs24 Mutect2\

\f2\b0\fs20 a tool to detect somatic variants using a panel of normals to account for systemic errors\
\

\f0\b calling variants:
\f2\b0 \
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx5913\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 $ gatk --java-options "Xmx2g" Mutect2		activate gatk Mutect2 and infuse java option 2GB of RAM
\fs26 \
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf0 	-R <hg19.fasta>					RefGen (with fasta, .fai and .dict)\
	-I <tumor.bam>					input1\
	-tumor <tumor @RG SM field value)		provide the read group for the tumor sample\
	-I <normal.bam>					input2 (if added after the \
	-normal <normal @RG SM field value)		provide the read group for the normal sample\
	-pon <pon.vcg.gz>					provide the prefiltered variant sites in a PanelOfNormals\
								pon.vcf has to be generated in previous step (see below)\
		\'97genotype-pon-sites			allow for variants that were detected in pon (default is filter out)								will be flagged as IN_PON in the INFO field\
	-germline-resource					database of variant alleles in a population\
								(eb. gnomad) \
		\'97af-of-alleles-not-in-resource <2e-10)		adjustment for the lower threshold of detectable allele freqs in the 								resource \'97> the more samples in the resource, the lower the value should 								be set ( ~1/(2 *exome_samples) \
	-L <region_list.txt>					restrict analysis to certain genomic intervals (bed file or region list)\
	\
	-bamout 						generate reassembled alignment file\
\
special options:\
 	- -disable-read-filter MateOnSameContigOrNoMappedMateReadFilter	\
								MOSCO filter removes reads that are mapped to different contigs\
								new aligners can well align over different contigs so you lose valid reads\
\

\f0\b creating the PoN annotation:\
	1)	
\f2\b0 run Mutect2 in tumor-only mode on the normal samples in the PoN-list\
		$ gatk Mutect2 -R <ref> -I <normal.bam> -tumor <@RG SM of normal> -O normal1.vcf.gz\
		optional but recommended: -germline-resource - -af-of-alleles-not-in-resource <0.0000025>\
	
\f0\b 2) 
\f2\b0 	concat all the normal annotations to a PoN annotation:\
		$ gatk CreateSomaticPanelOfNormals -vcfs <one of the normals from step 1)> -vcfs \'85\'85. -O <pon.vcf.gz>\
		
